# =============================================================================
# Stillnote .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: commit what a teammate needs to build, run and review the
# project; ignore anything that is generated, machine-specific, or private.
# Every entry below says which of those it is.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Secrets and local configuration  (PRIVATE - never commit)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env files hold database passwords, METRICS_TOKEN and SENTRY_DSN. A leaked
# secret stays in git history even after it is deleted, so these are blocked
# up front. The *.example files ARE committed: they document every variable
# with safe placeholder values, so a new developer knows what to configure.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Dependencies  (GENERATED - rebuilt from package-lock.json)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hundreds of megabytes that `npm ci` recreates exactly. Committing them would
# bloat the repository and include platform-specific binaries (argon2, esbuild).
node_modules/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Build output and tool caches  (GENERATED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Produced by `npm run build` and by CI / the Docker image build, so the
# committed source is the single source of truth.
client/dist/
client/dev-dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.vite/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Runtime data and user data  (PRIVATE + GENERATED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# server/data/ is the retired JSON note store from before PostgreSQL. It holds
# real notes, so it must not be published.
server/data/

# Database dumps made by ops/backup.sh contain every user's notes and password
# hashes. Keep them on backup storage, never in git.
backups/
*.dump


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Test and load-test artifacts  (GENERATED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright traces and screenshots can contain session cookies and note text.
# k6 summaries are regenerated by every `npm run loadtest`.
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
loadtest/results/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Logs  (GENERATED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Operating system and editor files  (MACHINE-SPECIFIC)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These differ per developer and say nothing about the project.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Local AI-assistant state  (MACHINE-SPECIFIC)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer permissions and caches, not project configuration.
.claude/settings.local.json
graphify-out/


# =============================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED - these look generated or private but must be
# committed, so do not add them above:
#
#   package-lock.json      Pins every dependency. CI and the Docker builds use
#                          `npm ci`, which fails without it, and it makes
#                          installs reproducible and auditable.
#   server/migrations/     The database schema history. Without it nobody can
#                          create or upgrade a database.
#   .github/               CI pipeline and Dependabot configuration.
#   .husky/pre-commit      The shared pre-commit hook. (.husky/_/ is generated
#                          by husky itself and is ignored by its own .gitignore.)
#   client/public/         Static files served as-is: icons, PWA assets,
#                          theme-init.js.
#   e2e/ and loadtest/     Test sources and seed data. Only their outputs
#                          (section 5) are ignored.
#   ops/ and scripts/      Backup/restore and local-CI scripts.
#   Dockerfile, nginx/,    How the app is built and deployed. Reviewed like code.
#   docker-compose*.yml
#   .prettierrc.json,      Formatting and lint rules shared by the whole team,
#   eslint.config.js       so style is not a matter of personal settings.
# =============================================================================
